    {
      "id": "claim_cfa7211182fa42f29ad44c0b598f1ead",
      "statement": "The timezone offset consumers are explicit and consistent: the clock segment converts the injected tz_offset_seconds to a time::UtcOffset via UtcOffset::from_whole_seconds and applies it to ctx.now when formatting the wall-clock time; render_line injects the offset from clock::detect_tz_offset, which reads the system local offset once cached in a LazyLock and falls back to 0 (UTC); and the TUI preview / fixed-clock tests inject 0 (UTC) for determinism. The offset is never read from the ambient environment inside render_line's callers.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/render/mod.rs#L23-L26",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:57aef1eefe67473d88b973cbdb54a49da3595792f0d1bb8f42089a117c8167b2:"
